  "id": "f278ae5a-95dc-53f4-8779-349233e916ee",
  "slug": "chimichurri-chicken-burgers-recipe-7553187",
  "name": "Chimichurri Chicken Burgers",
  "recipe_type": "main",
  "brief_description": "We fixed the chicken burger, and all it really took was stirring in a couple spoons of chimichurri sauce. It\u2019s one of the best burgers you\u2019ll ever have.",
  "cuisine": "Fusion",
  "instructions": [
    {
      "position": 1,
      "text": "To make the chimichurri: Chop herbs with a sharp knife until fine; add sliced garlic to the mixture. Continue chopping until mixture is very fine; transfer to a bowl. Stir in the 1/4 cup olive oil, white wine vinegar, the 1/4 teaspoon salt, black pepper, cumin, and red pepper flakes. Wrap and refrigerate until needed."
    },
    {
      "position": 2,
      "text": "To make the burgers: Place chicken thighs in the freezer until firm and half-frozen, about 30 minutes."
    },
    {
      "position": 3,
      "text": "Place thighs on a cutting board, and using a large sharp knife or heavy cleaver, chop until they resemble coarsely ground meat. (Alternatively, place chicken in a food processor; pulse on and off, scraping sides often, until texture resembles coarsely ground meat.)"
    },
    {
      "position": 4,
      "text": "Transfer chicken to a bowl, add the 1 \u00bd teaspoons salt and 1/4 cup chimichurri sauce. Use a fork to mix thoroughly."
    },
    {
      "position": 5,
      "text": "Using damp hands, form chicken mixture into 4 equal-sized patties, about 1/2-inch thick. Cover and refrigerate until chilled, about 30 minutes."
    },
    {
      "position": 6,
      "text": "Stir mayonnaise and remaining chimichurri sauce together to make spread for buns; refrigerate until needed."
    },
    {
      "position": 7,
      "text": "Remove burgers from the fridge; sprinkle both sides with bread crumbs."
    },
    {
      "position": 8,
      "text": "Add olive oil to a large non-stick skillet and set over medium high heat. When hot, but before oil starts smoking, add burgers, and cook about 5 minutes per side, or until chicken is cooked through. An instant read thermometer inserted near the center should read 165 degrees F (74 degrees C)."
    },
    {
      "position": 9,
      "text": "Let burgers rest for a minute or two. Serve on buns spread with chimichurri mayo and the fixings of your choice."
    }
  ],
  "servings": 4,
  "cooking_time_minutes": 10,
  "preparation_time_minutes": 20,
  "rest_time_minutes": null,
